00053FE0                            ; The reason I think this is an *early* SMPS 68k Type 1b
00053FE0                            ; is because this subroutine is the one from Type 1a:
00053FE0                            ; other Type 1b drivers have a newer, optimised version.
00053FE0                            ; The driver itself is Type 1b, with this odd exception.
